                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I do not think its a terrible game. [spoiler]I had to start the review like that, peer pressure and all.[/spoiler]\n\nAn archery tower defense, on a budget. Honestly, I was going to thumbs this down, but after discovering the price (I got this in a bundle), its a thumbs up by the skin of its teeth.\n\nPretty much every aspect of this could use some work. Sounds not great, the arrow is a little too finicky to nock, even in the short time I played it I came across issues (mobs got stuck inside the gate I was to defend and could not be shot - had to use a map-wide expensive ability to kill them), design choices not great (selecting towers to either build or upgrade requires you to shoot them, which starts to become a pain when you want to build on a far off one in the middle of your game).\n\nThere is potential, but it really does need more work. [b]I would recommend you wait to see if any patches drop for it.[/b] I cant see any activity at all for this from the devs - no patch info (if there was any) and the only thread currently on the forum regarding bugs has no dev responses. Again, only because they are not being greedy its a thumbs up, BUT if it receives no updates, I would suggest avoiding.",
